About 1.5 km off La Gaulette lies Île aux Bénitiers, a flat coral islet of some 65 hectares, once known as Île du Morne. Its beaches look straight across the lagoon to Le Morne Brabant, one of the classic views of the southwest.

There is little to do on the island itself apart from swimming, lazing in the shade and eating, which is exactly the point. Boat trips from La Gaulette and the neighbouring villages usually stop here, often together with the Crystal Rock and, early in the day, a look for dolphins.

## Good to know

- Bring reef shoes, water and sun protection: shade is limited.
- Take all your rubbish back with you.
